-- title:
--   Stalks under base change with unchanged residue field
-- statement:
--   Let $A_0$ and $A$ be local rings, $\iota : A_0 \to A$ a ring homomorphism that is local (it pulls the maximal ideal back to the maximal ideal) and such that the composite $A_0 \to A \to A/\mathfrak m_A$ is surjective. Let $X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ and $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$ be morphisms of schemes, and let $\mathrm{iso}$ be an isomorphism of $X$ with the pullback of $X_0 \to \operatorname{Spec} A_0$ along $\operatorname{Spec}\iota$ whose composite with the second projection is the given morphism $X \to \operatorname{Spec} A$. Let $x \in X$ lie over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} A$. Write $\mathrm{pr} : X \to X_0$ for $\mathrm{iso}$ followed by the first projection, and let $c : A \to \mathcal O_{X,x}$, $c_0 : A_0 \to \mathcal O_{X_0,\mathrm{pr}(x)}$ be the structure maps obtained from global sections and the germ maps at $\top$. The conclusion has four parts: (i) the stalk map of $\mathrm{pr}$ at $x$ carries $c_0(a)$ to $c(\iota a)$ for all $a \in A_0$; (ii) there is a ring isomorphism $\mathcal O_{X_0,\mathrm{pr}(x)}/\mathfrak m_{A_0}\mathcal O_{X_0,\mathrm{pr}(x)} \cong \mathcal O_{X,x}/\mathfrak m_A\mathcal O_{X,x}$ (quotients by the ideals generated by the images of the maximal ideals) compatible with the stalk map and the quotient maps; (iii) for ideals $Q, Q'$ of $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ with $Q'$ prime, both containing $\mathfrak m_A\mathcal O_{X,x}$, an inclusion of their contractions along the stalk map forces $Q \le Q'$; (iv) every prime $P$ of $\mathcal O_{X_0,\mathrm{pr}(x)}$ containing $\mathfrak m_{A_0}\mathcal O_{X_0,\mathrm{pr}(x)}$ is the contraction of some prime $Q$ of $\mathcal O_{X,x}$ containing $\mathfrak m_A\mathcal O_{X,x}$.
--
--   This records that base change along a local homomorphism inducing an isomorphism of residue fields leaves the special fibre, and hence the special-fibre stalks, unchanged: parts (iii) and (iv) together say that contraction along the stalk map is an order-preserving bijection between the primes over the respective base maximal ideals. It is used in the comparison of smooth loci for a scheme and its base change along a discrete valuation ring, in [`AlgebraicGeometry.mem_smoothLocus_iff_base_mem_smoothLocus_of_iso_pullback_of_isDiscreteValuationRing`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.mem_smoothLocus_iff_base_mem_smoothLocus_of_iso_pullback_of_isDiscreteValuationRing).
